workedExamples.question_text:
A rectangle has area $91\text{ cm}^2$ and length $13\text{ cm}$. Find its width.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (13,7);
\path (6.5,0) node[below] {$13\text{ cm}$};
\path (13,3.5) node[right] {width};
\path (6.5,3.5) node {$91\text{ cm}^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Compare the areas and perimeters of rectangles $18\text{ cm}$ by $5\text{ cm}$ and $15\text{ cm}$ by $6\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5mm,y=2.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (18,5);
\path (9,0) node[below] {$18\text{ cm}$};
\path (18,2.5) node[right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw[black] (27,0) rectangle (42,6);
\path (34.5,0) node[below] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\path (42,3) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Compare the perimeters and areas of rectangles $23\text{ m}$ by $4\text{ m}$ and $16\text{ m}$ by $11\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5mm,y=2.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (23,4);
\path (11.5,0) node[below] {$23\text{ m}$};
\path (23,2) node[right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[black] (32,0) rectangle (48,11);
\path (40,0) node[below] {$16\text{ m}$};
\path (48,5.5) node[right] {$11\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
These rectangles both have area $24\text{ cm}^{2}$.
Find the perimeter of each.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (6,0); \coordinate (C) at (6,1); \coordinate (D) at (0,1);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$}; \draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$2\text{ cm}$}; \draw (C) -- (D); \draw (D) -- (A);
\coordinate (E) at (8,0); \coordinate (F) at (11,0); \coordinate (G) at (11,2); \coordinate (H) at (8,2);
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ cm}$}; \draw (F) -- (G) node[midway,right] {$4\text{ cm}$}; \draw (G) -- (H); \draw (H) -- (E);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

These rectangles both have perimeter $20$ cm.
Find the area of each.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (4,0); \coordinate (C) at (4,1); \coordinate (D) at (0,1);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$}; \draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$2\text{ cm}$}; \draw (C) -- (D); \draw (D) -- (A);
\coordinate (E) at (6,0); \coordinate (F) at (8.5,0); \coordinate (G) at (8.5,2.5); \coordinate (H) at (6,2.5);
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ cm}$}; \draw (F) -- (G) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ cm}$}; \draw (G) -- (H); \draw (H) -- (E);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
